---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import graph from '../data/researchGraph.json';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
const internal = (segment) => `${base}/${segment.replace(/^\//, '')}`;
const nodeById = new Map(graph.nodes.map((node) => [node.id, node]));
const chain = graph.canonical_chain.map((id) => nodeById.get(id)).filter(Boolean);
const researchObjects = graph.nodes.filter((node) => ['paper', 'draft', 'institutional_proposal'].includes(node.type));
---
<Layout title="Provenance" description="A navigable record of how Agalmic Research ideas, papers and principles emerged, including human and machine contributions and epistemic status.">
  <header class="page-head">
    <div class="shell">
      <p class="eyebrow">Research provenance</p>
      <h1>Do not preserve only the answer. Preserve the path.</h1>
      <p class="lede">Agalmic Research records intellectual contribution separately from epistemic authority. The goal is a navigable graph of questions, ideas, criticisms, decisions, drafts and evidence rather than a flat author list.</p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell thesis">
      <p class="eyebrow">Chain currently under scrutiny</p>
      <blockquote>Cognitive abundance → authorial capacity gap → defensible stewardship → separable contribution and authority → epistemic handoff → epistemic uptake scarcity → institutions for routing knowledge.</blockquote>
      <p>This chain is a research hypothesis and genealogy, not a declaration that every link has been established empirically.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell split">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Session protocol</p>
        <h2>Capture the discovery process while it is happening.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="prose">
        <p class="large">The Agalmic Research Memory Palace Protocol initializes provenance, epistemic-authority, evidence, search-space and decision-replay tracking at the start of a research session.</p>
        <p>It requires each provenance-complete session to preserve not only selected conclusions but rejected, deferred, surfaced-but-unexamined and scope-excluded branches, together with reversal conditions and a search-boundary statement.</p>
        <div class="actions">
          <a class="button" href={internal('memory-palace-protocol')}>Read the protocol</a>
          <a class="button secondary" href={internal('downloads/Agalmic_Research_Memory_Palace_Protocol_v0.2.md')} download>Download v0.2 Markdown</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell split">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Two ledgers</p>
        <h2>Contribution is not authority.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="prose">
        <p class="large">A useful provenance system must answer two different questions.</p>
        <div class="status-grid">
          <div><strong>Contribution provenance</strong><span>Who initiated, framed, searched, generated, selected, developed, criticized, edited or realized the work?</span></div>
          <div><strong>Epistemic authority</strong><span>Who can defend which claims, and what expertise, evidence, verification, replication or formal support warrants that authority?</span></div>
        </div>
        <p>These records are deliberately independent. Originating an idea does not certify it. Validating an idea does not erase its origin.</p>
        <div class="callout"><p><strong>Origin deserves credit. Authority requires warrant.</strong></p></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="section-head">
        <span class="section-number">Canonical chain</span>
        <div class="section-copy">
          <h2>How the current argument developed.</h2>
          <p>Each stage is represented as a node in the research graph. Attribution is reconstructed from the September 2026 conversation and repository history and remains open to correction.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="index-list">
        {chain.map((node, i) => (
          <article class="index-item">
            <span class="index-meta">{String(i + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</span>
            <div>
              <h3>{node.label}</h3>
              <p class="muted">{node.summary}</p>
            </div>
            <span class="index-status">{node.epistemic_status}</span>
          </article>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell split">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Human + machine authorship</p>
        <h2>Record roles, not fictional symmetry.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>The present research sequence is neither accurately described as solely human-authored nor as machine-generated. Different intellectual acts have different provenance.</p>
        <p><strong>Human curator:</strong> repeatedly initiates core questions and intuitions, directs the search, accepts or rejects formulations, introduces new conjectures, prioritises the publication sequence and authorises publication.</p>
        <p><strong>OpenAI ChatGPT:</strong> materially contributes terminology, conceptual decomposition, synthesis, drafting, adversarial criticism, research structuring and the development of consequences from human-originated directions.</p>
        <p class="muted">The graph records these roles node by node. It does not imply equal contribution to every idea, and neither contribution record grants automatic epistemic authority.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="section-head">
        <span class="section-number">Research objects</span>
        <div class="section-copy">
          <h2>Papers and proposals carry their genealogy with them.</h2>
          <p>These objects currently have explicit contribution records in the graph.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="index-list">
        {researchObjects.map((node, i) => (
          <article class="index-item">
            <span class="index-meta">{String(i + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</span>
            <div>
              <h3>{node.label}</h3>
              <p class="muted">{node.summary}</p>
              {node.repository_path && <p><code>{node.repository_path}</code></p>}
            </div>
            <span class="index-status">{node.epistemic_status}</span>
          </article>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell split">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Machine-readable record</p>
        <h2>A graph, not merely a narrative.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>The human-readable page is a projection of a machine-readable graph containing actors, nodes, typed edges, contribution roles and epistemic status. Future tooling can render it as a navigable discovery map, attach conversations and evidence, and trace any published claim back toward its intellectual ancestors.</p>
        <div class="actions">
          <a class="button" href={internal('research-graph.json')}>View research graph JSON</a>
          <a class="button secondary" href="https://github.com/TsatsuAmable/agalmicresearch/blob/main/docs/RESEARCH_PROVENANCE_PROTOCOL.md">Read provenance protocol ↗</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell split">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Memory-palace direction</p>
        <h2>Eventually, walk the discovery process.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="prose">
        <p class="large">The long-term object is a navigable memory palace of research discovery.</p>
        <p>A reader should be able to enter at a paper, claim or principle and travel backward to the questions and conversations that produced it, sideways to rejected alternatives and criticism, and forward into experiments, software, institutions and later papers.</p>
        <p class="muted">The current graph is intentionally small. It establishes the chain of custody before we attempt richer visualization or automation.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
